  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (multimodal, SCVI, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 acc, which already shows that weighted fusion of SCVI RNA + ResNet50 image outperforms RNA-only SCVI (0.650), confirming the image modality adds value. The key remaining uncertainty is whether a stronger image encoder can further improve the fusion. config_037 (multimodal, SCVI, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted) is a single-variable change from config_031 (ResNet50 → imagenet_vit_l), cleanly isolating the effect of image encoder quality. ViT-L is substantially larger and pretrained on ImageNet, so it may extract richer spatial features that complement the SCVI RNA representation in weighted fusion. This is the best use of experiment 9 because it directly exploits the strongest configuration found so far while testing the most impactful unexplored axis (image encoder capacity), and with only 1 experiment remaining, a clean single-variable extension of the best result maximizes the chance of finding a new best."
